<title>JAPAN: Japan insurers' latent securities profits fall.</title>
<headline>Japan insurers' latent securities profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's top eight life insurance companies released data on Monday on their unrealised profits on securities holdings as of the end of March.</p>
<p>Unrealised profits on shareholdings were as follows, with comparisons with March 1996 (in billions of yen unless stated otherwise):</p>
<p>				 March 1997	 March 1996</p>
<p> Nippon Life		 4.03 trln	  5.16 trln</p>
<p> Dai-Ichi		    1.62 trln	  2.46 trln</p>
<p> Meiji			 1.34 trln	  2.17 trln</p>
<p> Sumitomo			473.6		934.4</p>
<p> Yasuda			  246.3		508.7</p>
<p> Asahi			   184.9		758.9</p>
<p> Mitsui			  139.1		484.2</p>
<p> Chiyoda			   4.9		196.8</p>
<p> TOTAL			  8.04 trln	 12.67 trln</p>
<p>The full names of the life insurers are Meiji Life Insurance Co, Asahi Mutual Life Insurance Co, Sumitomo Life Insurance Co, Dai-Ichi Mutual Life Insurance Co, Nippon Life Insurance Co, Mitsui Mutual Life Insurance Co, Yasuda Mutual Life Insurance Co, and Chiyoda Mutual Life Insurance Co.</p>
